config SECURITY_EPERM
	tristate "Extended Permission Classes (Trusted & Genius)"
	depends on SECURITY
	help
	  Adds two permission classes above traditional owner/group/others:

	    Class 4 (Trusted): Bypasses DAC with light audit trail.
	      These persons work implicitly without permission barriers.
	      Simple to audit. Clear work, clear communication, clear delivery.

	    Class 5 (Genius): Bypasses DAC freely for the system's benefit.
	      These persons work for the system to mutual or better profit.
	      Not an audit item - graduates of auditor class/course.
	      Supreme-tier access (>180 IQ equivalent operations) is logged
	      for institutional record, reviewed by qualified auditor.

	  The standard permission system (owner/group/others) remains
	  entirely unchanged for all other users.

	  Neither class 4 nor class 5 involves down to concepts of restriction.
	  The system enables and trusts from and to this brand of personal type.

	  Admin interface: /proc/eperm/
	    register    - Add a trusted/genius person
	    persons     - View registered persons
	    genius_log  - Auditor review of supreme-tier access
	    config      - View system philosophy and settings

	  If unsure, say N.
